@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Manual warmup
+
+The existing owner-authenticated `POST /panel/v2/quotas/warmup/:provider` route
+accepts `{ "dryRun": false, "force": true }` for `Claude`, `Codex`, and `Gemini`.
+Both flags are explicit: dryRun still defaults to true, force defaults to false.
+Without force the previous eligibility rules are unchanged.
+
+Manual force ignores automatic opt-in, the persisted five-hour cooldown, and
+whether the five-hour window is active or already started. It uses the saved
+model; it does not enable or reconfigure the scheduler. Gemini only uses the
+Gemini Models group on the AGY account. Claude still requires Haiku and passes
+allowActiveWindow to the existing verified CLI invocation.
+
+Force retains the durable attempt lock, active/unknown CLI-session checks,
+quota verification, subscription authentication, model restrictions, and CLI
+execution safeguards. A parallel attempt returns `locked`. As before, the
+lock serializes all providers, including calls from other adapter instances.
+Failures release the lock and allow another explicit forced attempt immediately.
+Attempts still reserve the automatic cooldown before inference and remain in
+history with trigger `manual`; scheduled calls cannot use force.
+
+A completed prompt consumes quota. It does not reset or increase provider limits.
+An HTTP timeout does not prove that no prompt was sent; callers should display
+an unconfirmed result rather than claim success. No live warmup is needed for
+the regression suite: `npm test` injects quota and CLI fixtures.
